  "summaries": {
    "en": "Terrain adaptation, EX Skill cost management, Total Assault raid strategies, and Pyroxene optimisation for Blue Archive.",
    "ja": "テレイン適性、EXスキルコスト管理、総力戦レイドの戦略、ピロキセン最適化を解説するブルーアーカイブ攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "rpg",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541701494587-cb58502866ab?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Terrain adaptation (Urban, Outdoors, Indoors) multiplies student damage by 1.2× (Advantage) or reduces it by 0.5× (Disadvantage)—always check raid terrain type and bring only Advantage or Neutral students.",
      "EX Skill cost (1–4 Cost) and the 4-cost-per-turn regeneration rate determine how frequently you can activate Special abilities—optimise your team to have at least 2 EX Skills at 2-cost or below to maintain continuous activation.",
      "Total Assault (raid) scoring is based on damage dealt within a fixed timer—the optimal raid strategy uses burst-damage compositions over sustained DPS, as the damage ceiling matters more than survivability.",
      "Pyroxene (premium currency) earned from Story completion, monthly missions, and raid participation exceeds Pyroxene from direct purchases for F2P players—complete story chapters before spending Pyroxene on gacha.",
      "Club membership provides passive daily income in credits and enhancement stones—join an active club with 25+ members and participate in club content to maximise passive income without active play."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "テレイン適性（市街地・野外・屋内）は生徒のダメージに1.2倍（有利）または0.5倍（不利）の倍率をかける。常にレイドのテレインタイプを確認し、有利または中立の生徒のみを連れてくる。",
      "EXスキルコスト（1〜4コスト）と毎ターン4コストの再生速度が特殊能力の発動頻度を決定する。継続的な発動を維持するために、少なくとも2つのEXスキルのコストが2以下になるようにチームを最適化する。",
      "総力戦（レイド）スコアは固定タイマー内のダメージに基づく。最適なレイド戦略は持続的なDPSよりもバーストダメージ構成を使用する。ダメージの上限は生存率より重要。",
      "ストーリー完了、月次ミッション、レイド参加から得られるピロキセン（プレミアム通貨）はF2Pプレイヤーにとって直接購入を上回る。ピロキセンをガチャに使う前にストーリーの章を完了する。",
      "クラブ加入はクレジットと強化石の受動的な日次収入を提供する。25人以上のメンバーを持つアクティブなクラブに参加し、アクティブなプレイなしで受動収入を最大化するためにクラブコンテンツに参加する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Early Student Priority",
        "body": "The tutorial provides free SR students covering basic archetypes. For early game, prioritise levelling a Healer student (Seia, Koharu, or any event-available healer) to level 40 first—healers prevent the game-over condition in longer story missions where DPS students are not yet strong enough for one-burst clears. Use Eligma (Student upgrade material) from raids to unlock EX Skill upgrades on your primary DPS student before upgrading support roles."
      },
      {
        "title": "Lesson and Equipment Farming",
        "body": "Equipment (Hairpins, Bags, Shoes, Watches, etc.) determines a student's stat total more than level—each tier of equipment upgrade adds 15–25% to a student's primary stat. Farm Equipment Stages (not EXP stages) until you have at least Tier 5 equipment on your primary team before investing in level-ups. The Equipment Difficulty (Hard mode stages) unlocks at player level 35 and provides the highest equipment tier drops per stamina spent."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Raid Team Composition Building",
        "body": "Build separate team compositions for each raid type—Total Assault raids change the featured boss and terrain monthly. Maintain at minimum: 1 Indoor team (for Indoor raid bosses), 1 Outdoor team, and 1 Urban team. Each team should have terrain-Advantage DPS as the primary damage source and a Cost-efficient Healer (2-cost EX) to prevent early wipes. Avoid building a single \"universal\" team—terrain penalties make universal teams score 40–50% lower than specialized terrain teams."
      },
      {
        "title": "Crafting and Eligma Management",
        "body": "Eligma (obtained from duplicate gacha pulls and specific missions) is used to upgrade student EX Skills and unlock character limit breaks. Reserve Eligma for your top 3 DPS students's EX Skill levels (target EX Level 5 for primary attackers). Never use Eligma on support students until your primary attackers are at EX Level 5—support EX upgrades have diminishing returns compared to primary attacker upgrades at the same Eligma cost."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Grand Assault and Extreme Modes",
        "body": "Grand Assault events feature multi-stage bosses with resetting HP—the score from each wave carries over. For Grand Assault optimization: identify which stage clears with exactly enough damage to trigger the wave end (leaving the boss at 1–5% HP before a wave clear is the most damaging inefficiency). Use the \"practice\" attempts to measure your team's total damage output before committing to ranked attempts. Extreme-difficulty Total Assault provides Platinum score tier rewards only achievable with a fully specialized terrain team."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Ignoring terrain adaptation and using favourite students regardless of terrain type—terrain disadvantage (-50% damage) makes even highly levelled and equipped students perform worse than low-level terrain-advantage students.",
      "Pulling gacha without saving for limited banners—Blue Archive limited Students are generally stronger than standard students; the meta periodically features limited students as top-tier raid performers.",
      "Levelling all students uniformly rather than concentrating on top teams—level 80 requires significantly more EXP and materials than level 60; level 3 students to 80 before levelling 10 students to 60.",
      "Not completing Daily Missions and Commissions—Daily missions provide the highest consistent Pyroxene income; missing them over a week costs the equivalent of one 10-pull in lost Pyroxene.",
      "Forgetting to collect Café passive income—the Café generates Momotalk Hearts passively over time; these Hearts unlock story episodes that provide Pyroxene; uncollected Hearts expire and cannot be reclaimed."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "テレイン適性を無視してテレインタイプに関係なく好きな生徒を使う。テレイン不利（ダメージ-50%）は、高レベルで装備が整った生徒でさえ、低レベルのテレイン有利の生徒よりパフォーマンスが劣る。",
      "限定バナーのために貯めずにガチャを引く。ブルーアーカイブの限定生徒は一般的に標準生徒より強い。メタは定期的にトップティアレイドパフォーマーとして限定生徒を特集する。",
      "トップチームに集中するのではなく全ての生徒を均一にレベルアップする。レベル80はレベル60より大幅に多くのEXPと素材が必要。10体の生徒をレベル60にする前に3体をレベル80にする。",
      "デイリーミッションとコミッションを完了しない。デイリーミッションは最高の一貫したピロキセン収入を提供する。1週間でそれらを見逃すと、失われたピロキセンで10回引き相当を失う。",
      "カフェのパッシブ収入を忘れる。カフェは時間の経過とともにパッシブでモモトークのハートを生成する。これらのハートはピロキセンを提供するストーリーエピソードをアンロックする。未収集のハートは有効期限が切れて取り戻せない。"
    ]
